schema: "0.3"
id: echo-of-manifestation-env-bleached-asylum
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  text: >
    Dark fantasy concept art of the Bleached Asylum — Zone 3 of the Twilight Zone. A vast
    institutional corridor rendered in sterile whites and pale grays that feel more hostile
    than any dark color. The walls are painted institution-green and white, peeling to reveal
    older layers of paint beneath — each layer a different era's attempt to make this place
    tolerable. Fluorescent lights flicker overhead in a long receding line, some dead, some
    strobing, casting harsh flat light that eliminates comfort. Medical equipment — gurneys,
    IV stands, restraint chairs — is fused with shadow, as if the darkness itself has grown
    into and through the metal, creating organic-dark extensions on clinical objects. Rust
    stains streak down the walls from ceiling fixtures like old tears. The floor is linoleum,
    cracked and curling, reflecting the fluorescent flicker. A long corridor stretches into
    distance, doors on both sides, some ajar revealing treatment rooms where shadow has
    consumed the furniture. The lighting is harsh institutional fluorescent — cold, flat,
    unflattering — a deliberate contrast to the warm amber of other zones. This zone's horror
    is clinical, sterile, dehumanizing. Painterly style but with cleaner architectural lines
    to match the institutional setting. The mood is medical horror — the violation of care
    turned to harm.
  negative: "bright, cheerful, cartoon, anime, clean magic, warm lighting, amber light, medieval, fantasy architecture, colorful palette, dirty gritty texture, low detail, flat shading, modern hospital"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024
    aspect_ratio: "3:2"

tags: [environment, zone-3, asylum, institutional, horror, concept-art, dark-fantasy]
